mvn clean removes the previous Maven build output, usually the target/ directory.
deleteDir() is a Jenkins Pipeline step that deletes everything inside the current workspace directory.

Example
stage('Cleanup') {
    steps {
        deleteDir()
    }
}

Suppose the Jenkins workspace contains:

workspace/
├── pom.xml
├── src/
├── target/
├── test-results/
└── old-file.txt

After:

deleteDir()

the workspace becomes empty:

workspace/
└── (empty)


mvn clean vs deleteDir
They are not the same.

Command	What it cleans
mvn clean	Maven build output, mainly target/
deleteDir()	Everything in the current Jenkins workspace
cleanWs()	Jenkins workspace cleanup; commonly used for workspace cleanup in post

